"Correlated correlation functions in random-bond ferromagnets (https://arxiv.org/abs/cond-mat/9911083)\nciteturn6academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 26.9 years ago; Title: Correlated correlation functions in random-bond ferromagnets\nTitle: Correlated correlation functions in random-bond ferromagnets\nAuthors: Tom Davis, John Cardy\nDate: Fri Nov  5 17:11:24 1999\n\nThe two-dimensional random-bond Q-state Potts model is studied for Q near 2 via the perturbative renormalisation group to one loop. It is shown that weak disorder induces cross-correlations between the quenched-averages of moments of the two-point spin/spin and energy/energy correlation functions, which should be observable numerically in specific linear combinations of various quenched correlation functions. The random-bond Ising model in (2+epsilon) dimensions is similarly treated. As a byproduct, a simple method for deriving the scaling dimensions of all moments of the local energy operator is presented.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nE-Preprints hep-th/9501 at DESY (https://www-library.desy.de/preparch/hep-th/9501/00index.html)\nciteturn6search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 31.8 years ago; Crawled: 19.9 years ago;     Title: Renormalisation group calculation of correlation functions for the 2D ... You can find the full abstract of hep-th/9501017 at the arXiv Preprint server. - (German mirror).\n     Paper: hep-th/9501017\n    From: picco(at)lpthe.jussieu.fr (Marco PICCO)\n    Date: Sat, 7 Jan 1995 18:14:41 +0100 (MET)   (16kb)\n    \n    Title: Renormalisation group calculation of correlation functions for the 2D\n      random bond Ising and Potts models\n    Authors: Vladimir Dotsenko, Marco Picco and Pierre Pujol\n    Comments: 26 pages, latex, no figures\n    Report-no: PAR--LPTHE 94/41\n    Journal-ref: Nucl.Phys. B455 (1995) 701-723\n    \\\\\n     \n\nThe complete Postscript Version of this paper is also available locally. However to conserve disk space this version might be \"staged\" to tape.\nAccess the local version of hep-th/9501017.\n\nN.B. You can find the full abstract of hep-th/9501017 at the arXiv Preprint server. - (German mirror).\n    \n     Paper: hep-th/9501018\n    From: aratyn(at)uic.edu\n    Date: Fri, 6 Jan 1995 15:44:53 -0700   (16kb)\n    Date (revised): Mon, 05 Jun 1995 18:02:39 -0500 (CDT)\n    \n    Title: Darboux-Backlund Solutions of SL(p,q) KP-KdV Hierarchies, Constrained\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCorrelated correlation functions in random-bond ferromagnets - ORA - Oxford University Research Archive (https://ora.ox.ac.uk/objects/uuid%3Ad5d3e53c-c02f-44d6-9540-95a906ec89dd)\nciteturn6search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 26.6 years ago; Crawled: 4 months ago; ## Correlated correlation functions in random-bond ferromagnets ... Correlated correlation functions in random-bond ferromagnets.\n\nImage: Journal article icon\n\n# Journal article\n\n## Correlated correlation functions in random-bond ferromagnets\n\nAbstract:\n    The two-dimensional random-bond Q-state Potts model is studied for Q near 2 via the perturbative renormalisation group to one loop. It is shown that weak disorder induces cross-correlations between the quenched-averages of moments of the two-point spin/spin and energy/energy correlation functions, which should be observable numerically in specific linear combinations of various quenched correlation functions. The random-bond Ising model in (2 + ∈) dimensions is similarly treated. As a byproduct, a simple method for deriving the scaling dimensions of all moments of the local energy operator is presented. © 2000 Elsevier Science B.V. All rights reserved.\n\nPublication status:\n    Published\n\n\n  * Cite\n\n# Cite this record\n\n## APA Style\n\nDavis, T., & Cardy, J. (2000). Correlated correlation functions in random-bond ferromagnets. NUCLEAR PHYSICS B, 570(3), 713–725.\n\nCopy APA Style [Input]\n\n## MLA Style\n\nDavis, T., and J. Cardy. “Correlated Correlation Functions in Random-Bond Ferromagnets.” NUCLEAR PHYSICS B, vol. 570, no. 3, 2000, pp. 713–25.\n\nCopy MLA Style [Input]\n\n## Chicago Style\n\nDavis, T, and J Cardy. 2000. “Correlated Correlation Functions in Random-Bond Ferromagnets.” NUCLEAR PHYSICS B 570 (3): 713–25.\n\n\n### Access Document\n\n* * *\n\nGenerating preview...\n\nPublisher copy:\n    10.1016/S0550-3213(99)00786-5\n\n### Authors\n\n* * *\n\n[Input] [Input]\n\n+ Davis, T More by this author\n\nRole:\n    Author\n\n+ Cardy, J More by this author\n\nRole:\n    Author\n\n### Bibliographic Details\n\n* * *\n\nJournal:\n    NUCLEAR PHYSICS B More from this journal\nVolume:\n    570\nIssue:\n    3\nPages:\n    713-725\nPublication date:\n    2000-03-27\nDOI:\n    \n\n10.1016/S0550-3213(99)00786-5\n\n### Item Description\n\n* * *\n\nLanguage:\n    \n\nEnglish\n\nKeywords:\n\n240734\n\nDeposit date:\n    \n\n2012-12-19\n\nARK identifier:\n    \n\nark:/29072/ora_d5d3e53cc02f44d6954095a906ec89dd\n\n### Terms of use\n\n* * *\n\nCopyright date:\n    2000\n\nLicence:\n    Terms and Conditions of Use for Oxford University Research Archive\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nProf John Cardy FRS: Publications | University of Oxford Department of Physics (https://www.physics.ox.ac.uk/our-people/cardy/publications?page=15)\nciteturn6search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago; Physics Letters, Section B: Nuclear, Elementary Particle and High-Energy Physics 483:1-3 (2000) 303-308 ... Details from ArXiV ... ### Correlated correlation functions in random-bond ferromagnets\n\nMore details from the publisher\n\nMore details\n\nDetails from ArXiV\n\n### Linking numbers for self-avoiding loops and percolation: application to the spin quantum hall transition.\n\nPhys Rev Lett 84:16 (2000) 3507-3510\n\n#### Abstract:\n\nNonlocal twist operators are introduced for the O(n) and Q-state Potts models in two dimensions which count the numbers of self-avoiding loops (respectively, percolation clusters) surrounding a given point. Their scaling dimensions are computed exactly. This yields many results: for example, the number of percolation clusters which must be crossed to connect a given point to an infinitely distant boundary. Its mean behaves as (1/3sqrt[3] pi) |ln( p(c)-p)| as p-->p(c)-. As an application we compute the exact value sqrt[3]/2 for the conductivity at the spin Hall transition, as well as the shape dependence of the mean conductance in an arbitrary simply connected geometry with two extended edge contacts.\n\nMore details from the publisher\n\nMore details\n\n### Correlated correlation functions in random-bond ferromagnets\n\nNuclear Physics B 570:3 (2000) 713-725\n\n#### Authors:\n\nT Davis, J Cardy\n\n#### Abstract:\n\nThe two-dimensional random-bond Q-state Potts model is studied for Q near 2 via the perturbative renormalisation group to one loop. It is shown that weak disorder induces cross-correlations between the quenched-averages of moments of the two-point spin/spin and energy/energy correlation functions, which should be observable numerically in specific linear combinations of various quenched correlation functions. The random-bond Ising model in (2 + ∈) dimensions is similarly treated. As a byproduct, a simple method for deriving the scaling dimensions of all moments of the local energy operator is presented. © 2000 Elsevier Science B.V. All rights reserved.\n\nMore details from the publisher\n\nMore details\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCorrelated correlation functions in random-bond ferromagnets (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/222658510_Correlated_correlation_functions_in_random-bond_ferromagnets)\nciteturn6search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 months ago; # Correlated correlation functions in random-bond ferromagnets ...   * Nuclear Physics B 570(3):713-725 ...   * This person is not on ResearchGate, or hasn't claimed this research yet.\nArticle\n\n# Correlated correlation functions in random-bond ferromagnets\n\n  * March 2000\n  * Nuclear Physics B 570(3):713-725\n\nDOI:10.1016/S0550-3213(99)00786-5\n\nAuthors:\n\nTom Davis\n\nTom Davis\n\n  * This person is not on ResearchGate, or hasn't claimed this research yet.\n\nJohn Cardy\n\nJohn Cardy\n\n  * This person is not on ResearchGate, or hasn't claimed this research yet.\n\n## Abstract\n\nThe two-dimensional random-bond Q-state Potts model is studied for Q near 2 via the perturbative renormalisation group to one loop. It is shown that weak disorder induces cross-correlations between the quenched-averages of moments of the two-point spin/spin and energy/energy correlation functions, which should be observable numerically in specific linear combinations of various quenched correlation functions. The random-bond Ising model in (2+ϵ) dimensions is similarly treated. As a byproduct, a simple method for deriving the scaling dimensions of all moments of the local energy operator is presented.\n\n## No full-text available\n\nImage: Request Full-text Paper PDF\n\nTo read the full-text of this research,\nyou can request a copy directly from the authors.\n\nRequest full-text PDF\n\n## Citations (17)\n\n## References (16)\n\n... To achieve such a result in a 3D 'simple' disordered system (simple as opposed to spin glasses, where the same fact has been recently established numerically for all values of the temperature in the broken phase [13]) is in some sense unexpected. However, indeed some important theoretical results achieved by Davis and Cardy, many years ago, have clarified the plausibility of this fact [14,15]. Conformal invariance allows crucial developments in critical scaling, starting from 2D systems [5]. ...\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCritical models of disorder in 2 spatial dimensions - INSPIRE (https://inspirehep.net/literature/1300060)\ncitetur